From: pmos-galaxy
Subject: [PATCH] dbm: create dumb buffers with 4096-byte rows

buffer_create() asked for height=size, width=1, bpp=8. omapdrm pads the
pitch to at least 8 bytes, so every buffer was 8x its size (4 MB -> 32 MB
for 1280x800 XRGB). Two triple-buffered window surfaces then exhausted the
SGX's VMArena ("MMU_Alloc: RA_Alloc of VMArena failed"), and mutter's
second surface got no colour buffer: GNOME rendered nothing. Use 4096-byte
rows; the overshoot is below one row.
---
--- a/dbm/dbm.c	2026-11-20 23:16:16.097022436 +0000
+++ b/dbm/dbm.c	2026-11-20 23:16:16.173021451 +0000
@@ -433,10 +433,16 @@
 
   TRACE("%s size %d, flags %x\n", __func__, size, flags);
 
+  /*
+   * Ask for 4096-byte rows. A size x 1 x 8bpp request makes drivers that pad
+   * the pitch (omapdrm: at least 8 bytes per row) allocate up to 8x the
+   * size, which exhausts the SGX's device-virtual heap (pmos-galaxy
+   * docs/bringup.md B18).
+   */
   create_dumb_req.flags = 0;
-  create_dumb_req.height = size;
-  create_dumb_req.width = 1;
-  create_dumb_req.bpp = 8;
+  create_dumb_req.width = 1024;
+  create_dumb_req.bpp = 32;
+  create_dumb_req.height = (size + 4095) / 4096;
 
   if (drmIoctl(fd, DRM_IOCTL_MODE_CREATE_DUMB, &create_dumb_req))
     return -errno;
